65 years of SCI — and a celebration that belonged to everyone who has been a part of this remarkable story.

Our deepest gratitude to Hon’ble Union Minister Shri Sarbananda Sonowal Ji and Hon’ble Minister of State Shri Nitesh Narayan Rane Ji for gracing the occasion, and to Shri Vijay Kumar, IAS, Secretary, MoPSW; Shri Mukesh Mangal, Additional Secretary, MoPSW; Shri Shyam Jagannathan, IAS, DGMA; Vice Admiral Sanjay Vatsayan, AVSM, NM, Flag Officer Commanding-in-Chief, Western Naval Command; esteemed Heads of Institutions; and all our distinguished guests from the maritime fraternity for being with us.

Beyond the stage and the spotlight, this evening was really about the people who have given SCI its soul — our seafarers, our employees, our families, and generations who have carried the Corporation through six and a half decades.

As Hon’ble Shri Sarbananda Sonowal Ji said, “As India works to become a top shipbuilding nation under Maritime Amrit Kaal Vision 2047, SCI’s fleet, its people and its partnerships will be central to that mission.”

With gratitude for the past, pride in the present, and faith in the India we are helping build, we look ahead — towards Viksit Bharat 2047.

Presenting a glimpse of an evening that belonged to the SCI family. ⚓

